    "narrative": "Our top-tier offensive outlook for today is headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (79.89) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), who both benefit significantly from park factors and favorable matchups against back-end rotation arms. **Corbin Carroll** is a lock despite a slight platoon drag, as his speed profile and the park elevation at Coors elevate his ceiling in our 5x5 format. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** sees a massive 10% boost from his venue, combined with a 12% boost from the SP skill profile of Tyler Mahle, making him a high-leverage start for power and RBI potential. **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) rounds out the top trio, gaining an impressive 14% boost from a favorable platoon split against Merrill Kelly, who also presents a soft target for potential stolen base opportunities given the slower delivery time.\n\nStrategic decision-making was most tested at the final utility spot, where **Vinnie Pasquantino** (68.38) narrowly edged out **Henry Bolte** (57.95). While **Henry Bolte** boasts a solid profile and would typically be a viable starter, the optimizer prioritized the sustained platoon edge and higher base projection of **Vinnie Pasquantino** against Dustin May. **James Wood** remains a high-floor cornerstone at 69.99; his lead-off spot against Shane Baz provides essential volume for Runs, and his elite 90% stolen base-friendly matchup is a critical component of our current category strategy.\n\nWe are monitoring the status of the lineup pending designations closely, particularly for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**, whose efficiency scores could swing if they fall further down the order. The biggest situational risk today is the matchup for **Brice Turang** (55.69); while he benefits from wind-out conditions, Joe Ryan\u2019s 3.41 xERA makes him the most dangerous pitcher on our slate, limiting the ceiling for the middle infield. We are keeping **Austin Riley** and **Zach McKinstry** on the bench for today's slate, as their current efficiency metrics fall below the 60.00 threshold required to displace the high-speed, high-platoon efficiency of our projected starters.",
